# Paths markdownlint-cli skips. It reads this file by default, so the
# `markdownlint` npm script and the lint-staged `--fix` hook use the same list.
# Syntax is .gitignore's: a pattern without a leading `/` matches at any depth,
# so the two root-only files below are anchored with one.
#
# `shared/tests/gate-ignores.test.ts` pins this: it drops a non-compliant file
# into each directory below and fails if markdownlint reports it — and fails
# if it stops reporting an un-ignored one, so it cannot pass vacuously.
#
# History: these lived in `.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc` until #189. Every
# directory entry there was once written with a bare trailing slash, which
# matched no file and silently ignored nothing (#128).

**/node_modules/**
**/dist/**
**/build/**
**/coverage/**

# Generated artifacts. Playwright writes Markdown failure contexts into
# test-results/, so without these a failing e2e run also fails the
# markdownlint gate and blocks the push.
**/test-results/**
**/playwright-report/**
**/reports/**
**/a11y-reports/**

# lychee-action writes its run summary to lychee/out.md inside the workspace
# before `check:all` runs, so CI lints a file whose format lychee controls,
# not us. Same failure shape as the Playwright contexts above.
**/lychee/**

# Claude Code agent worktrees: full checkouts of this repo living inside it,
# so their Markdown is a duplicate of files already linted here.
**/.claude/**

/CHANGELOG.md
/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
